WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:03.966
In this Cloud Minute I'm going to show you how to 
add an Uptime Check to your project.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:08.633
From the developer's console click Monitoring and then
click Dashboards &amp; alerts

00:00:08.633 --> 00:00:10.633
This is going to open up a new tab. 

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:14.133
You may need to enable monitoring if you haven't already for your project.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:17.133
Next to the words "Uptime Checks"

00:00:17.133 --> 00:00:20.133
click Create Check

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:23.133
I want to do an HTTP check against a URL

00:00:23.133 --> 00:00:27.333
I'm going to put in my hostname 
and I want to check the path index.html

00:00:27.333 --> 00:00:30.833
Just to make sure everything is working correctly I'm going to click test.

00:00:30.833 --> 00:00:33.833
And since I got a 200/OK I'm going to click save.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:36.833
If I want to be notified when my site goes down

00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:39.100
I need to create an alerting policy.

00:00:39.966 --> 00:00:41.800
There are several notification methods

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.300
available but I'm going to choose email.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:47.300
I click add notification and then type my email address.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:50.300
Once that done I can click save policy.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.133
Now that the policy is saved

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.633
I will be notified by email when my site goes down.

00:00:56.633 --> 00:00:58.500
I hope you found this helpful.

